        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(xai): apply request policy to video generation requests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users generating video with xAI could configure provider request policy, such as custom headers or proxy settings, but xAI video generation requests ignored that policy.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe xAI video provider now sanitizes `cfg.models.providers.xai.request` and passes it into the existing provider HTTP resolver used by the create, poll, and download flow. The change is limited to request policy wiring and leaves generation parameters, polling semantics, idempotency headers, and media parsing unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers who depend on configured provider transport policy can expect xAI video generation to honor those request settings. Default behavior is unchanged when no request policy is configured.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/xai/video-generation-provider.test.ts` passed: 19 tests.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --engine claude --model claude-fable-5 --thinking high` reported no accepted/actionable findings.\n\n### 2026-07-12 follow-up: local controlled request-policy proof\n\n- Commit `523f5999e4` fixes the review gap by passing the resolved xAI request policy through video create, poll, and generated-video download. The poll/download stages now use guarded provider fetches when `allowPrivateNetwork` or a dispatcher/proxy policy is configured, while preserving the existing unconfigured fast path and bounded xAI JSON/media readers.\n- Local focused proof: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/xai/video-generation-provider.test.ts` passed: 19 tests.\n- The focused regression now asserts the configured header, explicit private-network opt-in, and dispatcher policy are visible on all three changed stages: create submit, status poll, and generated-video download.\n- This is controlled local provider-path proof only. No live xAI API call was made and no real xAI account, proxy, or media generation was exercised.\n",
